{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am writing because we haven't seen any lab results come through our system from Quest since Tuesday. I checked the integration settings under the administrative tab, and everything looks connected on our end, but the incoming feeds are completely blank when I refresh the diagnostic queue. We tried rebooting the local terminal and verifying the account ID numbers with our lab rep, but results for a patient we tested earlier this week are still missing. Could someone please look into why this connection might be dropping?",
   "id": "gen-231",
   "subject": "Missing lab results feed from Quest"
  },
  {
   "body": "Patients are still complaining that they aren't getting text reminders for their visits tomorrow. I went into the notification settings, updated the schedule templates, and saved them twice, but the system keeps reverting back to the old default times. This is causing unnecessary no-shows and it's extremely frustrating to deal with when we are already busy.",
   "id": "gen-232",
   "subject": "Automated reminder settings not saving"
  },
  {
   "body": "To Whom It May Concern,\n\nWe are currently reviewing our quarterly financial metrics and require assistance with tracking and managing our recent volume of denied insurance claims. Could you please provide guidance on utilizing the built-in reporting tools to categorize these denials and attach the necessary clinical documentation for resubmission?\n\nSincerely,\nBilling Department",
   "id": "gen-233",
   "subject": "Assistance with insurance denial tracking and reporting"
  },
  {
   "body": "We need guidance on how to correct an electronic lab requisition order that was rejected due to a missing diagnosis code before we resubmit it to the reference lab.",
   "id": "gen-234",
   "subject": "Rejected electronic lab requisition"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi there, I tried to scan an outside paper lab report into a patient's chart this morning, but the system gave me an error message about the file format being too large. I tried shrinking the PDF down using a compression tool, but it's still not attaching correctly when I click the upload button in the documents tab. Can you let me know what size limit we are supposed to be using?",
   "id": "gen-235",
   "subject": "Error uploading scanned paper lab report"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am currently with patients waiting in rooms and need immediate help. Insurance remittances posted this morning have somehow been misapplied across multiple invoice lines for several accounts. Fix this right now so we can balance the ledger.",
   "id": "gen-236",
   "subject": "URGENT: Misapplied payments and remittance posting error"
  },
  {
   "body": "It appears the electronic prescribing module is completely down or failing across our workstation terminals, as none of our out-of-stock medication substitution alerts are loading.",
   "id": "gen-237",
   "subject": "Prescription module and medication alerts not loading"
  },
  {
   "body": "Dear Support Team,\n\nWe are experiencing validation errors when attempting to batch and generate our weekly insurance claims for electronic submission. Specifically, several encounter forms are flagging errors regarding secondary insurance policy fields that were previously accepted under the old format. Could you please review the attached error logs and advise on how to resolve these validation blocks before our clearinghouse submission deadline?\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nPractice Billing Office",
   "id": "gen-238",
   "subject": "Claim validation errors prior to clearinghouse submission"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, we are trying to send a new prescription electronically for a patient, but the system is throwing an error saying the pharmacy details are outdated. I checked the directory and tried updating the pharmacy ID, but the transmission still won't go through. Could you help us verify the pharmacy database connection so we can get this sent over?",
   "id": "gen-239",
   "subject": "Electronic prescription transmission error"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am really annoyed because all of my saved medication favorites and custom sigs disappeared after the latest software update ran last night. I tried recreating them from scratch, but it takes way too much time between patients. Can you please check if our preference lists can be restored from a backup?",
   "id": "gen-240",
   "subject": "Medication favorites missing after update"
  }
 ]
}
